{
  "_note": "Hand-built stand-in for a Homey Pro, carrying no household data. Every shape here was copied from a real capture; the quirks each part pins are listed below and are asserted in src/server/tools/*.test.ts. Payloads arrive from the hub as object maps keyed by id, which is why these are objects rather than arrays.",
  "_quirks": {
    "devices.dim": "units read '%' while min is 0 and max is 1, so 60 percent is 0.6. This is the percentage trap.",
    "devices.volume_set": "second capability with the same percentage trap, on a different device class.",
    "devices.target_temperature": "a genuine unit-bearing number with min, max and step, where clamping to the device range is the right answer.",
    "devices.thermostat_mode": "an enum capability carries its allowed values as {id, title} pairs.",
    "devices.settings": "a real device stores its account password here. Nothing in this server may ever project settings into a tool result.",
    "devices.images/ui/flags/data/iconObj": "pure noise that dominates the 4 KB average size of a real device record.",
    "devices.meter_power.consumed": "sub-capabilities are named with a dot, so a capability filter has to prefix match.",
    "devices.energyObj.cumulative": "marks a meter that only counts up and must never be averaged.",
    "devices.virtualClass": "the owner can override the device class; the override wins and the declared class is kept alongside.",
    "devices.available": "an unreachable device carries unavailableMessage and must not be written to.",
    "zones.parent": "a zone whose parent is not in the index must still appear in the tree, otherwise its devices vanish.",
    "flows.triggerCount": "firmware-computed and read-only, and it moves on every start.",
    "flows.broken": "firmware-computed; starting a broken flow always fails.",
    "apps.author.email": "app metadata carries contact details that have no business in a tool result."
  },

